    "updated_at": "2022-11-24T16:25:11Z",
    "body": "I think it's normal that when it's interrupted it will continue to fill the outgoing buffer a bit as it might not immediately get a connection close. And we don't actually track which bytes have been successfully delivered.\r\n\r\nBut going all the way to 100% does seem surprising, but it seems not all implementations are doing that in which case I'd consider this an implementation bug.\r\n\r\nThere's certainly nothing in the specification that supports that kind of behavior.",
